  "transcriber_notes": [
   "Printed as blocks of commodity columns each repeating the 1935-1938 stub (3 blocks for Imports, 3 for Exports); merged here into one row per year per part. Rows: 4 per part as printed.",
   "In the first Imports block the year stub is printed about half a line lower than the figures; 4 figure lines assigned to the 4 year labels in order. Oil/Benzine/Liquid Fuel columns are printed slightly lower than the columns to their left; again 4 entries per column assigned in order.",
   "Exports last block: the 1936 stub label is printed '1836' (misprint); the year is written as 1936 in the merged row since the other two Export blocks print 1936.",
   "Exports Fresh Fruits 1936: '489' followed by a small raised dot/speck, probably a blemish; transcribed as 489.",
   "Exports Pepper 1937 printed in parentheses '(313)'; Pepper 1938 printed '...' with a smudge.",
   "Imports Total: the 22 listed commodities sum to 86,143 / 74,196 / 91,655 / 81,925 against printed totals 101,727 / 108,754 / 110,044 / 111,824, so the Total covers items not listed (it equals the Import column of Table 2 for 1935-1938); cannot be reconciled from the table.",
   "Exports Total: all 24 columns sum to 192,069 / 172,468 / 202,177 / 187,136 vs printed 172,595 / 158,218 / 184,361 / 169,493. Excluding 'Other Domestic Products' (apparently not additive): 1935 reconciles; 1936 reconciles; 1937 reconciles only if the parenthesised Pepper (313) is also left out (184,361); 1938 parts sum to 170,008 vs printed 169,493 — does NOT reconcile (diff 515). 1938 cells re-read; transcribed as printed.",
   "Export totals differ from the Export column of Table 2 (e.g. 1935: 172,595 vs 169,711) — noted only."
  ],
